		{
			dependencies: ["67E8B8DCFC93F832"]
			description: [
				"&5Regrettably, items do not move themselves. Until I discover a spell for that, to bridge the gap between the Miner and the Builder, we are stuck with Couriers.&r"
				""
				"&5Think of them as pack mules in human shape. A novice Courier is weak and... unburdened by intelligence. Upgrade their hut to improve their muscle mass &a(the number of items they can carry)&r&5 and cognitive processing speed &a(the amount of requests they can keep track of a time.)&r"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&5They must be assigned to a Warehouse to function. Be advised: a Courier is loyal to one Warehouse alone. They will ignore the stockpiles of neighboring buildings even if they are empty. You can use this bureaucratic tunnel vision to organize your logistics.&r"
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "490628CE108A833A"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "7EFD224B4DFF2D7A"
