				type: "advancement"
			}]
			x: 1.5d
			y: -22.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["15B51FB56A64C303"]
			description: [
				"&5Cobblestone is the building material of peasants and desperate refugees. To distinguish yourself from the scum of the earth, build with refined materials. The Stone Smeltery processes raw earth: Cobblestone into Stone, Clay into Bricks or Terracotta, and Logs into Charcoal. They may even pop Chorus Fruit, should your tastes run eccentric.&r"
				""
				"&5You must explicitly teach the Smelter the recipes you desire and designate a fuel type.&r"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&5Do not neglect aesthetics. I once visited a rival's 'Grand Fortress' constructed entirely of unsmelted cobblestone. I asked him if the masons were on strike or if he was simply stacking debris until the garbage cart arrived. He declared war immediately. It was a short war; his walls were as weak as his taste.&r"
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "430475E11D259B74"
			rewards: [
				{
					exclude_from_claim_all: true
					id: "00154CD53E104DD5"
					table_id: 1287062647694046403L
					type: "choice"
				}
				{
					id: "4FBC37FDD0B5D6C9"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 10
				}
			]
			subtitle: "Build a Stone Smelter"
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "minecolonies:production/build_stone_smeltery"
				criterion: ""
				id: "1C4CC262377E767F"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			x: 1.5d
			y: -21.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["15B51FB56A64C303"]
			description: [
				"&5Raw ore is heavy, dirty, and useless until refined. The Smeltery designates a worker to process these ores into ingots.&r"
				""
				"&5Upgrading this building should be your first priority. Higher levels allow the Smelter to utilize more furnaces simultaneously. More importantly, advanced facilities increase yield efficiency, offering a chance to double or triple the ingot output per ore. Only a novice accepts a mere one-to-one return.&r"
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "6A60B76053393288"
			rewards: [
